usage: cairn [-h] [--db PATH] [--bundle PATH] [--pin PATH] [--attest PATH]
             [--log LEVEL] [--version] [--robot-help]
             COMMAND ...

positional arguments:
  COMMAND
    attest              create and append to the operator-owned, append-only
                        attestation file
    bundle              compile, pin and inspect the content-addressed gate
                        bundle
    capabilities        describe the CLI contract: commands, exit codes, env
                        vars, paths
    env                 report the toolchain (python, cypari2/libpari, blake3,
                        gp path)
    gate                run the gate bundle's declarative plan of planted-
                        failure self-tests before any gate is trusted
    kat                 run the canonicalizer known-answer vectors (a gate
                        self-test); exit 2 on any mismatch
    measure             measure a skill's cost constant (toy-curve-tries:
                        tries and subprocess wall over seeds 1..N per size)
    robot-docs          print the paste-ready agent handbook
    selftest (self-test)
                        run a skill's vendored known-answer corpus and record
                        its certificate; exit 2 on any failure
    startup-scan        move every attempt left RUNNING by a dead harness to
                        INTERRUPTED before any new launch

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --db PATH             substrate SQLite file
  --bundle PATH         gate bundle SQLite file
  --pin PATH            gate-bundle pin file
  --attest PATH         attestation file
  --log LEVEL           log level for the JSON records on stderr
  --version             print the version and exit
  --robot-help          print the agent handbook (same as: cairn robot-docs)

Structured output: add --json to any read-side command. Contract: cairn
capabilities --json. Agent handbook: cairn robot-docs.
